>  <SELECTION_REASON>
Site-by-site g-xTB correction of ligand connectivity. Both the original same-ID connection table and NBO graph show C(CH₃)₂OH on the vinyl side chain. In the original XYZ, hydroxyl O7 and saturated C40 are 1.437 Å apart, g-xTB 0.910; Adding a C–O single bond gives tetravalent carbon and neutral OH. Rh(III) balances two monoanionic dimethylglyoximate ligands and a vinyl anion. Localized 18 aromatic-ring bonds using WBOs and original bond lengths.

